<title>USA: IVAX gets FDA OK for generic estazolam.</title>
<headline>IVAX gets FDA OK for generic estazolam.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>IVAX Corp said Monday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has approved an abbreviated new drug application for the generic pharmaceutical product estazolam in one milligram and two milligram tablets.</p>
<p>The company said estazolam is indicated for the short-term management of insomnia and is the generic equivalent of Abbott Laboratories Inc's Prosom.</p>
<p>The company said the product will be marketed by IVAX's Zenith Goldline Pharmaceuticals Inc unit.</p>
